ul.li:
a runnable slot is claimed with a single Xtensa
        S32C1I compare-and-swap, so exactly one core owns a
        task at a time;

a yielding task writes its resume address back and releases its
        slot; either core may pick it up next, so a task can move between
        cores at a yield unless it is pinned;

esp32_body_smp_contention.jal: two yielding
        tasks race across both cores with per-task duplicate-run detectors
        and a per-core claim counter;

esp32_body_smp_control.jal: pause, resume, kill
        and restart issued from a task while the target runs on the other
        core;

esp32_body_smp_affinity.jal: constant and
        variable pins hold (a task's last core matches its pin) while both
        cores claim tasks;
